  "name": "Cant de la Sibil·la (Mallorcan Christmas Sibyl chant)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Cant de la Sibil·la is a medieval chant of the Last Judgement, sung in Catalan at Christmas Eve Matins in Palma Cathedral and in parish churches across Mallorca. A boy or girl in a tunic, holding a sword, sings the verses alone and unaccompanied, with organ interludes between the stanzas; Mallorca kept the chant after the Council of Trent suppressed it in most places, and UNESCO has inscribed it as intangible heritage. The credited-organ card stands for the church organ.",
